% Refusal is a first-class result. Every one of these fails cleanly and whole,
% with a position, so the caller can fall back to the evaluator.

### name: refuse.abort-is-an-effect-not-a-value
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
ABORT("nope")
--- error
E_SQL_UNSUPPORTED 1:1
===
### name: refuse.list-in-scalar-position
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
(1, 2) + 1
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:2
===
### name: refuse.list-returning-function
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
INDEXES("a")
--- error
E_SQL_UNSUPPORTED 1:1
===
### name: refuse.aggregate-needs-stage-two
--- note
M3. Until then this is refused like anything else that cannot be translated,
which is the behaviour a caller depends on rather than a placeholder.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
ALL((1, 2, 3), _ > 0)
--- error
E_SQL_UNSUPPORTED 1:1
===
### name: refuse.no-truthiness-in-a-condition
--- note
Silently accepting WHERE o.total is how a database turns a validation rule
into the truthiness test SEL spent its whole design avoiding.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- as
condition
--- bindings
{"T": {"kind": "column", "column": "t", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
T
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE
===
### name: refuse.no-truthiness-in-and
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"T": {"kind": "column", "column": "t", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
T AND TRUE
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:1
===
### name: refuse.unknown-kind-may-be-a-condition
--- note
The other side of the same rule: an undeclared column may well be boolean, and
the database is the one that knows. It is wrapped rather than trusted.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- as
condition
--- bindings
{"F": {"kind": "column", "column": "flag"}}
--- source
F
--- expect
(`flag`) IS TRUE
===
### name: refuse.relation-binding-used-as-a-value
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ITEMS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "order_items", "alias": "oi", "fields": {"QTY": {"column": "qty", "type": "NUM"}}}}
--- source
ITEMS > 1
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:1
===
### name: refuse.columns-binding-used-as-a-value
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"V": {"kind": "columns", "items": [{"column": "a", "type": "NUM"}, {"column": "b", "type": "NUM"}]}}
--- source
V > 1
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:1
===
### name: refuse.unknown-field-of-a-relation
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ITEMS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "order_items", "alias": "oi", "fields": {"QTY": {"column": "qty", "type": "NUM"}}}}
--- source
ITEMS["price"] > 1
--- error
E_SQL_BINDING 1:6
===
### name: refuse.alias-collision
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"A": {"kind": "relation", "from": "x", "alias": "t"}, "B": {"kind": "relation", "from": "y", "alias": "t"}}
--- source
1 + 1
--- error
E_SQL_BINDING
===
### name: refuse.indexing-a-plain-column
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"T": {"kind": "column", "column": "t", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
T[1]
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:2
